Performance is over budget or at best unverified. stills.mjs printed 987–2223 ms per frame at --scale 1: avg 1743 ms on a 9-frame sample at load ≈3.5, and 1.0–2.2 s at load ≈6. The budget is ≤900 ms. The in-page bench (dev/bench-entry) shows the JS is cheap (renderMain <135 ms, thermal grid ≈30 ms). The time goes to raster and compositing:
- the full-frame 1080×1920 additive canvas of about 14k polylines;
- two full-frame bloom upscales;
- the WebGL water layer under it until f482;
- per-glyph CSS blur filters;
- the CSS drop-shadow filters on the ×7000 span and the 过程 canvas.

